{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874343-homebrew-vampire-holy-grail","id":874343,"title":"[Homebrew] Vampire: Holy Grail","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-26T01:33:24-07:00","id":874343,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [Homebrew] Vampire: Holy Grail","content":"So I got bored one night and thought about Vampire: Requiem. Personally, I don't like the lore. Nor the coventants. Nor the clans. And especially the changes in 2ed. I do like the mechanics, then why not make a world that I would gladly play and/or ST in, but doesn't give me a brain aneurysm every time I read about the Strix. So here is my try, the link is at the bottom to the doc, where you can comment, if you want. Feel free to call me an asshole for disliking your game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In short, this is the lore substitution for the clans, coventants and adds a history to the whole vampiric curse. It all starts with King Arthur finding the Grail and taking it back home. In the end, greed overcomes Arthur and he drinks from it, thus cursing himself and others that drink next. The vampires today are descendant of the Five Knights who drank after King Arthur and were transformed. There\u2019s betrayal, lies and politics, as every faction wants to explain their situation differently. In the end, they are all stuck in the city of King Arthur, because the curse doesn\u2019t let them leave. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1YShEFoiSTu0sAMmTKMh40qjOiKXUUi75gscSkofXfKM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11156-havoclivekiller","name":"Havoclivekiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T05:28:32-07:00","id":874429,"title":"","content":"Could be fun.<br /> One thing I really like about Requiem is the scrapping of the whole Masquerade meta-story. You could always run with your own history/setting/etc but Requiem encourages it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:02:09-07:00","id":874631,"title":"","content":"I think what you have is a perfectly fine thing for a couple of Kindred to believe in, but, I mean, for it to be the entire mythos? I can't really get behind that. It's too...simple, known, and kind of goofy. Don't get me wrong, I don't like the Strix, either, and have always totally ignored them, but I really like the core clans and covenants as they are:<br /> <br /> &quot;We don't know the answer&quot; is a lot more interesting to me than &quot;Oh, here's the answer. It's about King Arthur. There's no mystery to your condition.&quot;<br /> <br /> The covenants, especially, are great the way they are. The establishment. The rebels. &quot;Being a vampire is totally natural and cool.&quot; &quot;Being a vampire is terrible, but we have a mission.&quot; &quot;Being a vampire is pretty awesome, but the curses side of it sucks--let's fix that.&quot; I don't see why that's enough.<br /> <br /> And I have to ask: what about all the people who drank from the Grail between the Last Supper and Arthur? Nobody did? There are no other vampires anywhere? Why were there vampire myths in thousands of cultures throughout history, including/especially before the time of Arthur? If nobody can leave, why were they global after him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":". 04-26-2016, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T23:30:18-07:00","id":875349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think what you have is a perfectly fine thing for a couple of Kindred to believe in, but, I mean, for it to be the entire mythos? </div> </div> </div>t's not for the entire mythos. I've made it so the curse is local and can't spread over to other places. That the vampires in the city are the &quot;only&quot; ones in the world (also you need to take into account that real vampire mythos is different from what vampires in V:tR act and look like). This removes the strange notion that every Covenant somehow travels even when the feel of the game should be &quot;local politics.&quot; That's just bizarre, if not stupid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;We don't know the answer&quot; is a lot more interesting to me than &quot;Oh, here's the answer. It's about King Arthur. There's no mystery to your condition.&quot; </div> </div> </div>And that's fine with me. Personally I also like mystery, but how they handled the mystery in V:tR for me is half-assed. If they ditched a lot of stuff, made the system/setting more toolbox, then maybe I would be behind the whole &quot;you make your own mythos.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The covenants, especially, are great the way they are. </div> </div> </div>Some people like them, some people don't. For me they range from meh, okay to &quot;lol nope&quot;. Just the matter of preference. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I have to ask: what about all the people who drank from the Grail between the Last Supper and Arthur? Nobody did? </div> </div> </div>Maybe somebody did, but this is the story of King Arthur's Holy Grail. Where this pious, valorous and holy-than-thou man finds one of the most holiest of holy and his inner greed comes out. He gets cursed and, for lack of a better word, shares this curse with his followers, after seeing the powers he got from it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are no other vampires anywhere? Why were there vampire myths in thousands of cultures throughout history, including/especially before the time of Arthur? If nobody can leave, why were they global after him? </div> </div> </div>There might be some creatures that were called vampires that appeared in Europe, but Vampires or Kindred are only one - those descendant from King Arthur, that are confined to a small place in England.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11156-havoclivekiller","name":"Havoclivekiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:12:57-07:00","id":876038,"title":"","content":"Glad you found a way to make the game work for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}